    heading: "Human-in-the-loop: quotes, refunds and anything that commits your business",
    paragraphs: [
      `We design every automation around one question: what happens when the AI is wrong? For a meeting summary, a person reads it anyway and an error costs little. For a quotation sent to a customer, a refund, a contract clause or an answer about health or law, an error can cost money or trust, so a person approves before anything leaves the company. These are the controls we use.`,
